   I would like to propose the following system (comments more than welcome!)

a) Stormbringer can only drain 100 levels per 1000 turns (I'm not sure about
  100 being the right number,it needs play testing) after this the sword is
  deemed satiated and keeps its other abilities but no longer drains levels.

b) When a level is drained Stormy passes on 3 hit points to the weilder.These
  heal the weilder if they are below their max hit points or else increase
  their hit points to a maximum of 50 above their max hit points.Note that max
  hit points are not affected and any hit points above max will decay at a rate
  of 1 hit point per turn.

c) If Stormbringer is not used to drain at least 20 levels per 1000 turns then
  it gets hungry and you attack the next monster you are next to ,whether you
  like it or not.Similarly if you use it to drain more than 80 levels in the
  last 1000 turns then it takes control and forces you to hit the next monster
  coming next to you (this happened to Elric when he killed e.g. Rackhir).

 On another tack, I wish to had my voice to the people who think all characters
should be allowed to weild whatever weapon they damn well like,and that they
should not be disadvantaged doing this.The arguments about priests not being
allowed to use edged weapons and wizards only being able to use daggers just do
not hold water.As someone has already pointed out Gandalf in the The Lord of the
Rings weilded Glamdring ,the mate of Orcrist.Also clergy in medieval(sp?)
England were known to take up swords and ride in to battle,especially those who
were the third or fourth son of some noble family who had been put into the
church.Another example is the monks of many eastern religions who will take up
a martial art (including sword martial arts) as part of their search for
enlightenment (I'm not going into reasons for this now).Finally Elric wasn't
a bad mage or fighter now was he?
 As for wizards spending all their time studying magic,well I have time to do a
martial art and study at university,and if I didn't play Nethack (not likely!)
then I would probably have time to train in martial arts enough to get quite
good at them.
